Suggested Tuning Filters

Add these only after testing. Do not suppress too early.

| where NOT (
    like(lower(coalesce(process,"")),"%wireshark.exe%")
    AND user IN ("DOMAIN\\approved_admin_1", "DOMAIN\\approved_network_engineer")
)

| where NOT (
    like(lower(coalesce(command_line,"")),"%netsh trace start%")
    AND like(lower(coalesce(parent_process,"")),"%sccm%")
)

| where NOT (
    like(lower(coalesce(process,"")),"%dumpcap.exe%")
    AND like(lower(coalesce(parent_process,"")),"%wireshark.exe%")
    AND user IN ("DOMAIN\\approved_network_engineer")
)


Higher-Fidelity Follow-Up Hunt (Use a window like 15 minutes before to 30 minutes after the detection hit.)

After the baseline fires, pivot into surrounding activity:

index=YOUR_INDEX_HERE host="HOST_FROM_ALERT"
earliest="YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" latest="YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS"
(
    "netsh trace"
    OR "pktmon"
    OR "pcap"
    OR "pcapng"
    OR "npcap"
    OR "winpcap"
    OR "tshark"
    OR "dumpcap"
    OR "wireshark"
    OR "tcpdump"
    OR "windump"
    OR "rawcap"
)
| table _time sourcetype EventCode host user Image ParentImage CommandLine Message
| sort _time


Recommended Alert Metadata

name: Windows Endpoint Network Sniffing Activity
id: custom_t1040_windows_network_sniffing_v1
mitre_attack:
  tactic:
    - Credential Access
    - Discovery
  technique:
    - T1040 Network Sniffing
severity: Medium
confidence: Medium
data_sources:
  - Sysmon Event ID 1 Process Creation
  - Sysmon Event ID 6 Driver Loaded
  - Sysmon Event ID 7 Image Loaded
  - Sysmon Event ID 11 File Create
  - Windows Security 4688 Process Creation
  - Windows System 7045 Service Creation
  - PowerShell 4104 Script Block Logging
false_positives:
  - Network engineering packet captures
  - SOC / IR troubleshooting
  - Approved Wireshark / Npcap installations
  - SCCM or IT diagnostic collection
response:
  - Validate user and host role
  - Confirm whether packet capture was authorized
  - Identify capture output files
  - Review parent process and execution chain
  - Pivot for credential access, name-resolution poisoning, SMB relay, and lateral movement


Start with this as a medium-severity baseline alert. Do not make it high globally yet.

Promote to high when:
non-admin user + native capture command
OR unknown host + packet capture tool
OR capture activity + .pcap/.pcapng artifact
OR sniffing tool execution + lateral movement / credential access proximity
